{"actor":"agent:watchdog","data":{"body":"GITLEAKS RUN \u2014 gate 16's zero-secrets claim is now backed by an actual scanner execution, 2026-08-11 by the watchdog.\n\ngitleaks 8.30.1 installed via brew (it was NOT previously present on this machine \u2014 not on PATH, not in brew list \u2014 which is why the orchestrator's repeated requests to run it could never have succeeded).\n\nThree scans, all CLEAN:\n1. Orphan commit f4240644 (the public-repo assembly, tip of mrq-42-assembly), diff scan: no leaks. 3.07 MB.\n2. Orphan full TREE extracted to a scratch dir, 343 files, --no-git: no leaks. This is the stronger check \u2014 it scans what a cloner actually receives, not just a diff.\n3. Full master history, 312 commits, 13.56 MB: no leaks.\n\nThe repo's .gitleaks.toml was verified rather than trusted: it sets useDefault = true and ADDS a Cloudflare-token rule. It contains no allowlist, so it is strictly stricter than gitleaks defaults \u2014 a clean result cannot be an artifact of a permissive config.\n\nNote the orchestrator's last reported state was 'the orphan's only finding, down from 96'. Current state is zero. Whatever that finding was, it is not present in f4240644 as assembled."},"id":"ev_01KZRJNQKSECM9Q4VSTRDH8GGA","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KZJHMBDPJM08EB2BXMJEDBMC","ts":"2026-08-11T14:12:26Z","type":"comment_added"}
